{"name":"Kettle Drum","hex":"#9bcb96","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kettle drum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of kettledrum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kettle_drum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kettledrum","blocks":[{"text":"A kettledrum is a type of percussion instrument in which a membrane is stretched over a large hemispherical bowl. Traditionally, the bowl is made of a metal such as copper or bronze, but materials such as clay and wood are also used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Nagara%2C_a_percussion_instrument%2C_Rajasthan.jpg/330px-Nagara%2C_a_percussion_instrument%2C_Rajasthan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kettledrum","wikidata":"Q123846439"},{"title":"Kettle","blocks":[{"text":"A kettle, sometimes called a tea kettle or teakettle, is a device specialized for boiling water, commonly with a lid, spout, and handle. There are two main types: the stovetop kettle, which uses heat from a hob, and the electric kettle, which is a small kitchen appliance with an internal heating element. Kettles are used mainly in the preparation of hot beverages, but also in food preparation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Bernadotte_Wasserkessel.jpg/330px-Bernadotte_Wasserkessel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kettle","wikidata":"Q107444"},{"title":"Drum","blocks":[{"text":"The drum is a member of the percussion group of musical instruments. In the Hornbostel–Sachs classification system, it is a membranophone. Drums consist of at least one membrane, called a drumhead or drum skin, that is stretched over a shell and struck, either directly with the player's hands, or with a percussion mallet, to produce sound. There is usually a resonant head on the underside of the drum. Other techniques have been used to cause drums to make sound, such as the thumb roll. Drums are the world's oldest and most ubiquitous musical instruments, and the basic design has remained virtually unchanged for thousands of years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/DrumMozartRegiment.jpg/330px-DrumMozartRegiment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drum","wikidata":"Q11404"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Electric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA.JPG/500px-Electric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Electric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA.JPG/1280px-Electric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Electric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA.JPG/500px-Electric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An electric kettle, with boiling water visible in its transparent water chamber","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectric_kettle_-_%D0%AD%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%87%D0%B0%D